<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:32:default:windows">
<!--
    sharedpush-regparm: a declared parameter list the callee's own code
    contradicts is no evidence that a pushed slot is shared.
    wine's MSVCRT_longjmp (msvcr70.dll 0x10014d30, MinGW GCC) calls the static
    msvcrt_local_unwind2 with its three arguments in EAX, EDX and ECX, but the
    debug information lists them as ordinary parameters, so the declared list
    places a parameter on the padding slot `push edx; push edx` leaves after
    IsBadReadPtr. The sharedpush rule took that parameter as proof the slot is
    an argument on both arms and gave it to the undeclared `call eax` too,
    which printed `(*jmp->UnwindFunc)(jmp,frame)`; the callee pops one slot.
    Stage / sub-stage: P4 call-site input recovery (`check_call_double_use`,
    `p4_calls/kuna_sharedpush.rs`). A strict fix, always on.
    The fixture `sharedpush_regparm_pe_i386.exe` is assembled from
    `sharedpush_regparm_pe_i386.asm` (see the fixtures README). local_unwind
    and stack_free are declared here the way debug information declares them.
    0x401060 is the longjmp shape: the call through jmp->unwind takes jmp alone
    (1-2). 0x401040 pushes p above a branch for stack_free, whose code reads
    its stack argument, and for a call through a register: both still take p
    (3-4).
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/sharedpush_regparm_pe_i386.exe</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>map function r0x401000 local_unwind</com>
  <com>map function r0x401030 stack_free</com>
  <com>parse line extern void local_unwind(int *frame,int level,void *ebp);</com>
  <com>parse line extern void stack_free(int *p);</com>
  <com>load addr 0x401060</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load addr 0x401040</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="SHAREDPUSH-REGPARM #1: the call through the unwind slot takes the buffer alone" min="1" max="1">\(\*\(\(code \*\*\)v1\)\[9\]\)\(v1\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="SHAREDPUSH-REGPARM #2: it is never handed the padding slot" min="0" max="0">\)\(v1,[^)]*\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="SHAREDPUSH-REGPARM #3: stack_free keeps its push" min="1" max="1">stack_free\(a1\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="SHAREDPUSH-REGPARM #4: the call through the register takes it too" min="1" max="1">\(\*a0\)\(a1\);</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
